    {
      "slug": "lahmacun-term",
      "term": "Lahmacun",
      "definition": "A thin Turkish flatbread topped with spiced minced lamb and vegetables, cooked at high heat and eaten rolled around fresh salad."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe makes 4 flatbreads and takes 30 minutes to prepare, 30 minutes for the dough to rest and 20 minutes to cook. Thin rounds of dough are spread with a spiced lamb and vegetable paste and baked at the highest temperature your oven will reach until the edges are crisp and the topping is cooked through. Eat rolled up around fresh salad, squeezed with lemon."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: the topping paste must be very finely processed and spread as thinly as possible. A thick topping stays raw in the middle while the edges overcook. Pulse rather than blend to keep some texture."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
